FRE LAUNCH v0.5.10 Windows preview: one controlled retry after preflight and workflow fixes.
Date: 2026-11-02.
Confirmed from previous run 41468386731: 18/18 frontend tests and Vue/TS passed; Rust client compiled. The failure was an unsupported Tauri 2.5.0 --no-sign option.
This revision uses the supported createUpdaterArtifacts:false config override and only valid CLI options. Preflight now checks Vue, Vite production build, all frontend tests and Tauri build help BEFORE compiling the native engine. A pinned-engine cache is saved immediately after a successful engine build and checked by SHA-256, source commit and license on reuse.
Keep signed auto-update unchanged. Only upload an unsigned NSIS preview if Windows build, Microsoft Defender scans and clean-install launcher smoke test succeed.
